==English==

===Etymology===
Morphologically {{suffix|en|mistake|n<id:past participle>}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/mɪˈsteɪkən/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-mistaken.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪkən|s=3}}

===Verb===
{{head|en|verb form}}

# {{past participle of|en|mistake|nocat=1}}
#: {{ux|en|I'm frequently '''mistaken''' for my brother.}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[erroneous|Erroneous]].
#: {{ux|en|A '''mistaken''' sense of loyalty.}}
# {{lb|en|with a copula verb|often|with ''about''}} Having an [[incorrect]] [[belief]].
#: {{ux|en|I think you must be '''mistaken'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|He admitted he was '''mistaken''' about the budget numbers.}}

====Usage notes====
* The phrase {{m|en|if I'm not mistaken}} (and variations) is used to indicate that one is uncertain about something one has said.

